    "b-70-provider-capabilities-each-column-is-a-registe-3": {
      "id": "b-70-provider-capabilities-each-column-is-a-registe-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Each column is a registered provider id (the value you set as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "provider:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " in a\nworkflow or "
        },
        {
          "insert": ".archon/config.yaml",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "). A ✅ means Archon translates the corresponding\ncapability for that provider; a ❌ means the capability is unsupported. Unsupported\nbehavior is feature-specific: some optional fields are ignored with a warning, while\nstrict contracts fail closed. In particular, a node naming "
        },
        {
          "insert": "mcp:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "skills:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " or\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "plugins:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " on a provider without that capability fails the run before any node\nstarts, and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "context.resume",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rejects an explicitly unsupported provider at load\ntime and an implicitly resolved one at runtime. An "
        },
        {
          "insert": "mcp:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " declared "
        },
        {
          "insert": "optional: true",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "\ninstead runs the node without its servers and records why."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-70-provider-capabilities-the-columns-are-the-prov-4": {
      "id": "b-70-provider-capabilities-the-columns-are-the-prov-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The columns are the providers built from this repository. Release binaries install\nClaude, Codex and Pi as provider plugins, with the same capabilities. A third-party\nprovider plugin declares its capabilities in its install-time descriptor and is not\na column in this generated table. The same pre-spend capability checks apply."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-70-provider-capabilities-reporting-flags-describe-5": {
      "id": "b-70-provider-capabilities-reporting-flags-describe-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Reporting flags describe SDK fields that Archon translates into execution results.\nSupported does not guarantee that every result reports a value or that usage includes\nall nested agents. Unsupported fields remain absent; Archon does not estimate cost,\ncount events as turns, or substitute the requested model for an unreported model.\nCost reporting is independent of spend-limit support. Older providers may omit\nreporting declarations; absence means unknown, not unsupported."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-70-provider-capabilities-background-work-report-6": {
      "id": "b-70-provider-capabilities-background-work-report-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Background work: "
        },
        {
          "insert": "reported",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " waits for runtime-reported task endings; "
        },
        {
          "insert": "none",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " means verified absent;\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "unobserved",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " means background work may exist without an observable lifecycle. A process\nbackgrounded inside a foreground shell command ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "cmd &",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ") is invisible to every provider.\nCodex observes subagents through "
        },
        {
          "insert": "subAgentActivity",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " notifications and unified-exec processes\nthrough "
        },
        {
          "insert": "commandExecution",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " items with source "
        },
        {
          "insert": "unifiedExecStartup",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Idle thread status is\nnot evidence that this work has ended. See "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Streaming event mapping",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "docs/20-implementation/10-contributing/50-adding-a-community-provider.md",
              "section": "streaming-event-mapping",
              "label": "Streaming event mapping"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "\nfor the background-start admission and observation cutoff rules."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
